    "https://recruit.apo.ucla.edu/JPF11272": {
      "title": "Recruit",
      "description": "Pediatric Imaging Fellowship 2028-2029 (JPF11272) - UCLA Academic RECRUIT Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Pediatric Imaging Fellowship 2028-2029 (JPF11272) Pediatric Imaging Fellowship 2028-2029 Apply now to Pediatric Imaging Fellowship 2028-2029 Job #JPF11272 Radiological Sciences / David Geffen School Of Medicine / UCLA Position overview Position title: Pediatric Imaging Fellow Salary range: $103,390 - $131,141 Review timeline: 11/1/2026 Application Window Open date: September 1, 2026 Next review date: Tuesday, Aug 31, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Tuesday, Aug 31, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date. Position description The section of Pediatric Radiology at UCLA offers a one-year ACGME approved fellowship position for the 2027-2028 academic year and is currently recruiting applicants for the 2028-2029 academic year. The section is staffed by six full-time board certified radiologists (including Peds/MSK, Peds/Neuro, and Peds/IR trained faculty). The Mattel Children's Hospital has 115 dedicated Pediatric beds (93 pediatric, 23 neonatal), the outpatient care facility also includes a children's clinic and pediatric radiology installations. Over 70,000 examinations are performed per year in general pediatric imaging as well as, pediatric fluoroscopic exams, ultrasound, computed tomography, magnetic resonance imaging, PET-CT, and non-vascular interventional radiology. Pediatric Neuroradiology and Sports Medicine MRI training, as well as pediatric interventional procedures, Fetal MRI are included in the curriculum, while DCVI is an optional rotation. The posted Resident/Fellow salaries by GME ( Medical Resident Income | UCLA Medical School ) per CIR/SEIU bargaining agreement set the pay determined by PGY level at appointment. Department : https://www.uclahealth.org/radiology/ped-fellowship Qualifi