    "https://recruit.apo.ucla.edu/JPF11346": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty PositionApply nowto Adjunct Faculty Position",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Position (JPF11346) - UCLA Academic RECRUIT Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Adjunct Faculty Position (JPF11346) Adjunct Faculty Position Apply now to Adjunct Faculty Position Job #JPF11346 Anesthesiology & Perioperative / David Geffen School Of Medicine / UCLA Position overview Position title: Assistant Adjunct Professor Salary range: The salary range for this position is $126,800 - $148,000 based on step. Please refer to the posted UC salary scale T5 3 . Application Window Open date: September 18, 2026 Next review date: Friday, Oct 16, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Saturday, Oct 31, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description Position description The Department of Anesthesiology and Perioperative Medicine at UCLA is seeking a qualified candidate for an Adjunct Assistant Professor position to direct pre-clinical and translational research at the intersection of sex differences, vascular biology, and heart failure in pulmonary arterial hypertension (PAH). This role requires a strong investigator who will furthermore manage collaborative projects with multidisciplinary research teams and industry partners, mentor trainees at the graduate- and post-graduate levels, as well as track record of competitive extramural grant funding. Additionally, the candidate will oversee regulatory compliance, including IACUC animal protocols, lab inspections, and environmental biosafety standards. Candidates must hold a Ph.D. degree in molecular biology in the cardiovascular science field. Interested applicants should apply by submitting a CV and a UCLA Mission Statement to UCLA Academic Recruit at: Browse Open Recruitments or Log In - UCLA Academic RECRUIT The salary range for this position is: All inquiries may be sent to: Anesthesiology Academic Personnel AnesAP@mednet.ucla.eu The University of California is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. For the complete University of California nondiscrimination and affirmative action policy, see University of California nondiscrimination and affirmative action policy. Qualifications Basic qualifications • Ph.D. degree in molecular biology, with a focus on cardiovascular disease • Extensive background in both pulmonary and systemic vascular biology, alongside deep expertise in myocardial biology and the molecular mechanisms of left- and right-ventricular failure. This includes but is not limited to in vitro models (isolation of adult cardiomyocytes and cardiac fibroblasts, isolation of primary vascular cells, co-culture models),  and in vivo models (chronic angiotensin/isoproterenol infusion, myocardial ischemia/reperfusion injury, atherosclerosis) . • Proven background in sex differences research within cardiovascular disease, with a focus on the preclinical models of pulmonary arterial hypertension (Sugen/Hypoxia, Monocrotaline, Bleomycin, diet-induced PH) in sex-dimorphic genetic rodent models (Four Core Genotypes and Sry-modified rats). • Direct experience analyzing clinical datasets combined with effective project management and cross-functional communication with clinical research investigators. • Direct experience with effective project management and cross-functional communication with industry partners. • Proven track record in securing competitive extramural funding, alongside demonstrated excellence in mentoring, teaching, and supervising research trainees (graduate students and postdoctoral fellows). • Regulatory & Administrative Compliance: Direct experience with writing, managing, and overseeing animal utilization protocols (IACUC/DLAM) and Biosafety protocols, in addition to managing triennial renewals, regulatory inspections such as controlled substances/DEA, and maintaining strict compliance with laboratory biosafety and environmental health standards. Application Requirements Document requirements • Curriculum Vitae - Your most recently updated C.V. • Cover Letter • Statement of Research • Up to 3 key papers exemplifying the applicant’s research accomplishments • Reference check authorization release form - Complete and upload the reference check authorization release form • UCLA Mission Statement - As the nation's premier public research university, UC's mission is the creation, dissemination, preservation and application of knowledge for the betterment of our global society. We have a particular responsibility to the people of California which we express in the excellence of the education we provide, the impact of the research we do, the comprehensive, life-saving medical services we provide, and the public service mission we are devoted to. The University of California promotes the social mobility of its students, equips them with the tools and experience that furthers their ambitions, and regards their accomplishments across the life span as evidence of the profoundly positive impact of higher education. Prompt for candidates for recruitment: Reflecting on your personal and professional experiences, highlight your past contributions and future commitments to advancing UCLA's mission. These accomplishments and ambitions may be discussed in the context of describing your teaching, creative scholarly activity, and service • Statement of Teaching Reference requirements References will not be required at the time of application. Qualifications Basic qualifications • Ph.D. degree in molecular biology, with a focus on cardiovascular disease • Extensive background in both pulmonary and systemic vascular biology, alongside deep expertise in myocardial biology and the molecular mechanisms of left- and right-ventricular failure. This includes but is not limited to in vitro models (isolation of adult cardiomyocytes and cardiac fibroblasts, isolation of primary vascular cells, co-culture models),  and in vivo models (chronic angiotensin/isoproterenol infusion, myocardial ischemia/reperfusion injury, atherosclerosis) . • Proven background in sex differences research within cardiovascular disease, with a focus on the preclinical models of pulmonary arterial hypertension (Sugen/Hypoxia, Monocrotaline, Bleomycin, diet-induced PH) in sex-dimorphic genetic rodent models (Four Core Genotypes and Sry-modified rats). • Direct experience analyzing clinical datasets combined with effective project management and cross-functional communication with clinical research investigators. • Direct experience with effective project management and cross-functional communication with industry partners. • Proven track record in securing competitive extramural funding, alongside demonstrated excellence in mentoring, teaching, and supervising research trainees (graduate students and postdoctoral fellows). • Regulatory & Administrative Compliance: Direct experience with writing, managing, and overseeing animal utilization protocols (IACUC/DLAM) and Biosafety protocols, in addition to managing triennial renewals, regulatory inspections such as controlled substances/DEA, and maintaining strict compliance with laboratory biosafety and environmental health standards. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter (Optional) Statement of Research Reference check authorization release form -   Complete and upload the reference check authorization release form UCLA Mission Statement -   As the nation's premier public research university, UC's mission is the creation, dissemination, preservation and application of knowledge for the betterment of our global society. We have a particular responsibility to the people of California which we express in the excellence of the education we provide, the impact of the research we do, the comprehensive, life-saving medical services we provide, and the public service mission we are devoted to. The University of California promotes the social mobility of its students, equips them with the tools and experience that furthers their ambitions, and regards their accomplishments across the life span as evidence of the profoundly positive impact of higher education. The UCLA campus has expressed these goals in its strategic plan as follows: Deepen our engagement with Los Angeles Expand our reach as a global university Enhance our research and creative activities Elevate how we teach Become a more effective institution Prompt for candidates for recruitment: Reflecting on your personal and professional experiences, highlight your past contributions and future commitments to advancing UCLA's mission as embodied in the 2023-28 strategic plan. These accomplishments and ambitions may be discussed in the context of describing your teaching, scholarship, and service Up to 3 key papers exemplifying the applicant’s research accomplishments Statement of Teaching Reference requirements Selected candidates will be asked to provide references as part of the academic appointment process. Apply link: https://recruit.apo.ucla.edu/JPF11346 Help contact: cherrythongthavikiat@mednet.ucla.edu About UCLA As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time.  Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment, discrimination, dishonesty, or unethical conduct, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment Job location Los Angeles, CA Apply now to Adjunct Faculty Position or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Los Angeles is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Los Angeles is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic RECRUIT Personnel System University of California, Los Angeles Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
