    "https://recruit.apo.ucla.edu/JPF10946": {
      "title": "Project Scientists (Open Rank) (JPF10946)",
      "description": "Project Scientists (Open Rank) (JPF10946) - UCLA Academic RECRUIT Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Project Scientists (Open Rank) (JPF10946) Project Scientists (Open Rank) Apply now to Project Scientists (Open Rank) Job #JPF10946 Electrical Engineering / Henry Samueli School Engr & Ap / UCLA Position overview Position title: Assistant Project Scientist, Associate Project Scientist, Project Scientist Salary range: $100,400 - $139,900 Application Window Open date: October 14, 2026 Next review date: Tuesday, Jun 1, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description UCLA Samueli School of Engineering Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering Open Rank Project Scientist – Assistant, Associate, and Full Position Description The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) at the UCLA Samueli School of Engineering invites applications for an open-rank Project Scientist position at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Project Scientist level. Rank will be determined based on the candidate's qualifications, experience, and professional accomplishments. The department seeks highly motivated individuals to contribute to ongoing and emerging research initiatives across a broad range of areas within electrical and computer engineering. Areas of research may include, but are not limited to, artificial intelligence and machine learning, computer engineering, communications and signal processing, circuits and embedded systems, semiconductor devices, photonics, electromagnetics, robotics, control systems, and other related fields. Successful candidates will work independently and collaboratively with faculty, researchers, students, and interdisciplinary research teams to advance the department's research objectives. Responsibilities Responsibilities may vary depending on the research program, assigned projects, and appointment rank, and may include: Conduct independent and collaborative research in specialized areas of electrical and computer engineering. Design, develop, and implement research methodologies, experiments, computational models, and analytical approaches. Analyze and interpret research findings and contribute to the preparation of scholarly publications, technical reports, and presentations. Contribute to the development of research proposals, grant applications, and other activities supporting externally funded research programs. Collaborate with faculty, research staff, graduate students, and external partners to achieve project objectives. Provide technical expertise and research guidance to students and other members of the research team, as appropriate. Present research findings at academic conferences, professional meetings, and other scientific forums. Support the coordination and execution of research activities, including project planning, documentation, and reporting. Maintain high standards of research integrity, safety, and compliance with applicable University policies and sponsor requirements. Qualifications Basic Qualifications (Required at Time of Application) Ph.D. or equivalent doctoral degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or a closely related field. Additional Qualifications Demonstrated research experience in a field relevant to electrical and computer engineering. Ability to conduct research independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary environment. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and technical communication skills. Demonstrated ability to contribute to scholarly publications, research presentations, or other scientific outputs. Qualifications and research accomplishments appropriate to the proposed appointment rank. Rank Considerations Assistant Project Scientist Candidates at the Assistant Project Scientist rank are expected to demonstrate the ability to make meaningful contributions to research projects, exercise independent scientific judgment, and develop a record of research accomplishments appropriate to their career stage. Associate Project Scientist Candidates at the Associate Project Scientist rank are expected to have an established record of research accomplishments, demonstrated expertise in their field, and the ability to independently undertake significant research responsibilities and contribute to the advancement of research programs. Project Scientist (Full Rank) Candidates at the Full Project Scientist rank are expected to demonstrate a substantial record of research accomplishments, advanced expertise in their area of specialization, and a high level of independence in conducting and advancing complex research activities. Candidates should have a demonstrated ability to make significant contributions to established or emerging research programs. Appointment Information Appointments will be made at the Assistant Project Scientist, Associate Project Scientist, or Full Project Scientist rank, commensurate with the selected candidate's qualifications and experience. Positions may be full-time or part-time, depending on programmatic needs and funding availability. Appointments are subject to applicable University of California policies and procedures governing the Project Scientist series. The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. Qualifications Basic qualifications Basic Qualifications (Required at Time of Application) Applicants must hold a Ph.D. or equivalent doctoral degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or a closely related field, or have an equivalent combination of education and research experience appropriate to the Project Scientist series. Applicants must demonstrate research experience in an area relevant to electrical and computer engineering, with qualifications and scholarly accomplishments appropriate to the Assistant Project Scientist, Associate Project Scientist, or Full Project Scientist rank. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter (Optional) Statement of Research (Optional) Reference check authorization release form -   Complete and upload the reference check authorization release form UCLA Mission Statement -   As the nation's premier public research university, UC's mission is the creation, dissemination, preservation and application of knowledge for the betterment of our global society. We have a particular responsibility to the people of California which we express in the excellence of the education we provide, the impact of the research we do, the comprehensive, life-saving medical services we provide, and the public service mission we are devoted to. The University of California promotes the social mobility of its students, equips them with the tools and experience that furthers their ambitions, and regards their accomplishments across the life span as evidence of the profoundly positive impact of higher education. The UCLA campus has expressed these goals in its strategic plan as follows: Deepen our engagement with Los Angeles Expand our reach as a global university Enhance our research and creative activities Elevate how we teach Become a more effective institution Prompt for candidates for recruitment: Reflecting on your personal and professional experiences, highlight your past contributions and future commitments to advancing UCLA's mission as embodied in the 2023-28 strategic plan. These accomplishments and ambitions may be discussed in the context of describing your teaching, scholarship, and service Statement of Teaching (Optional) Reference requirements Applicants must provide the names and contact information of three professional references who can speak to their research experience, scholarly accomplishments, technical expertise, and qualifications for the position. References may be contacted during the selection process. Apply link: https://recruit.apo.ucla.edu/JPF10946 Help contact: mrevillame@seas.ucla.edu About UCLA As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time.  Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment, discrimination, dishonesty, or unethical conduct, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment Job location Los Angeles, CA Apply now to Project Scientists (Open Rank) or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Los Angeles is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Los Angeles is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic RECRUIT Personnel System University of California, Los Angeles Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
