    "https://recruit.apo.ucla.edu/JPF11427": {
      "title": "Project Scientist",
      "description": "Project Scientist - Biological Chemistry - Gonen Lab (JPF11427) - UCLA Academic RECRUIT Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Project Scientist - Biological Chemistry - Gonen Lab (JPF11427) Project Scientist - Biological Chemistry - Gonen Lab Apply now to Project Scientist - Biological Chemistry - Gonen Lab Job #JPF11427 Biological Chemistry / David Geffen School Of Medicine / UCLA Position overview Salary range: $79,400 - $209,000 Application Window Open date: October 27, 2026 Next review date: Friday, Nov 27, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Friday, Nov 27, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date. Position description The Department of Biological Chemistry is recruiting for an Assistant Project Scientist position in Professor Gonen’s laboratory. This position is intended for collaborative research working MIcroED method development with special emphasis on small molecule, membrane and soluble proteins, sample preparation and analyses. The Gonen lab has pioneered the MicroED method and seeks to keep developing this cryoEM method using top of the line equipment and important biological samples. The qualifications for this position are as follows: • Ph.D. in biochemistry, chemistry, materials science, bioengineering, or a closely related field of study. • Prior experience in macromolecular MicroED sample preparation and data analyses. • Prior experience in small molecule MicroED sample preparation and data analyses. • Prior publications in MicroED is a must. Job responsibilities include supporting the PI in the design and execution of funded projects, including preparation of samples for MicroED (macromolecular and small molecules, materials etc), optimization of parameters for MicroED including all aspects of sample preparation, data collection, data archiving and management, microscope optimization, data analysis, structure solution, pipeline optimization, paper writing and submission, grant writing, mentoring and teaching other lab members, writing budget and progress reports as required, day-to-day tasks related to project management, supervising graduate/undergraduate students, other postdoctoral fellows and technicians in the group as needed and engaging in collaborations as directed by the PI. Qualifications Basic qualifications Ph.D. in biochemistry, chemistry, materials science, bioengineering, or a closely related field of study. Prior experience in small molecule and macromolecular MicroED sample preparation and data analyses. Prior publications in MicroED is a must. Preferred qualifications First-author publication in MicroED Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter (Optional) Reference check authorization release form -   Complete and upload the reference check authorization release form UCLA Mission Statement -   As the nation's premier public research university, UC's mission is the creation, dissemination, preservation and application of knowledge for the betterment of our global society. We have a particular responsibility to the people of California which we express in the excellence of the education we provide, the impact of the research we do, the comprehensive, life-saving medical services we provide, and the public service mission we are devoted to. The University of California promotes the social mobility of its students, equips them with the tools and experience that furthers their ambitions, and regards their accomplishments across the life span as evidence of the profoundly positive impact of higher education. The UCLA campus has expressed these goals in its strategic plan as follows: Deepen our engagement with Los Angeles Expand our reach as a global university Enhance our research and creative activities Elevate how we teach Become a more effective institution Prompt for candidates for recruitment: Reflecting on your personal and professional experiences, highlight your past contributions and future commitments to advancing UCLA's mission as embodied in the 2023-28 strategic plan. These accomplishments and ambitions may be discussed in the context of describing your teaching, scholarship, and service Reference requirements 2-3 required (contact information only) Applicants must provide the names and contact information of their references Apply link: https://recruit.apo.ucla.edu/JPF11427 Help contact: kdserrano@mednet.ucla.edu About UCLA As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time.  Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment, discrimination, dishonesty, or unethical conduct, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment Job location Los Angeles, CA Apply now to Project Scientist - Biological Chemistry - Gonen Lab or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Los Angeles is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Los Angeles is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic RECRUIT Personnel System University of California, Los Angeles Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.apo.ucla.edu/JPF11426": {
      "title": "Lecturers (Physical Geography): UCLA Department of Geography AY 2026-2027 (JPF11426)",
      "description": "Lecturers (Physical Geography): UCLA Department of Geography AY 2026-2027 (JPF11426) - UCLA Academic RECRUIT Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Lecturers (Physical Geography): UCLA Department of Geography AY 2026-2027 (JPF11426) Lecturers (Physical Geography): UCLA Department of Geography AY 2026-2027 Apply now to Lecturers (Physical Geography): UCLA Department of Geography AY 2026-2027 Job #JPF11426 GEOGRAPHY / L&S Social Sciences / UCLA Position overview Position title: Lecturer Salary range: See Table 15 for the salary range for this position. A reasonable estimate for this position is $73,817-$78,314. Application Window Open date: October 28, 2026 Next review date: Friday, Jan 1, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Monday, Mar 15, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Geography at UCLA invites applications for part-time positions as a non-tenure track lecturer for physical geography courses. Responsibilities will include teaching, conducting regularly scheduled office hours, writing and grading exams, and supervising readers and teaching assistants. Materials will be accepted and reviewed on a rolling basis through 3/15/2027, for Winter, and Spring quarters to support the department’s scheduling and planning needs. Lecturer appointments are assigned according to the instructional needs of the Department of Geography and may be established quarter by quarter as dictated by the Strategic plan of the Department Chair. Applicants must demonstrate a record of effective undergraduate teaching. Positions will be filled when needed so applicants are encouraged to submit materials as early as possible. A Ph.D. in Geography or closely related field, and excellent teaching, communication and interpersonal skills are required. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Please submit your cover letter; curriculum vitae; copy of Ph.D. certificate or diploma; statement of teaching; teaching evaluations; sample syllabus; and the contact information for three references. Please submit your online application and required documents using this link . The University of California is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age or protected veteran status. See the complete University of California nondiscrimination and affirmative action policy, see UC Nondiscrimination & Affirmative Action Policy . This position is represented by the University Council – American Federation of Teachers: universityofcalifornia.edu . Internal applicants will be considered for reappointment prior to the consideration of external applicants. About UCLA As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. • “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment, discrimination, dishonesty, or unethical conduct, as defined by the employer. • UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy • UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties • APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment Qualifications Basic qualifications Ph. D. is required by date of hire. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter (Optional) Copy of Syllabus Statement of Teaching (Optional) Reference check authorization release form -   Complete and upload the reference check authorization release form Evidence of Doctorial Degree (Ph.D.) -   If your diploma is not available, please provide an official letter from the Dean or Registrar of your academic institution. Reference requirements 3-5 required (contact information only) Reference letters will be requested for candidates who are under serious consideration. Apply link: https://recruit.apo.ucla.edu/JPF11426 Help contact: emilykristina@geog.ucla.edu About UCLA As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time.  Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. The University of California is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected status under state or federal law. As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment, discrimination, dishonesty, or unethical conduct, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment Job location Los Angeles, CA Apply now to Lecturers (Physical Geography): UCLA Department of Geography AY 2026-2027 or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Los Angeles is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Los Angeles is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic RECRUIT Personnel System University of California, Los Angeles Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
